sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant B as Browser
    participant G as Gateway
    participant I as identity-service
    participant DB as identity DB
    participant K as Kafka

    U->>B: email or phone + password
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/login (public path)
    G->>G: rate limit 15/s per address, burst 40
    G->>I: forward
    opt Human check is on
        I->>I: verify Turnstile token with Cloudflare
    end
    I->>DB: find user by email or phone
    alt unknown user, wrong password, or locked
        I->>DB: failed counter +1, lock 15 min at 5
        I-->>B: 401 invalid credentials / 403 locked
    else status INACTIVE or BLOCKED
        I-->>B: 403 account not active
    else password ok
        I->>DB: reset failed counter
        alt single-session policy REPLACE
            I->>DB: mark older refresh tokens REPLACED
        else policy DENY and another session is active
            I-->>B: refused
        end
        I->>DB: store refresh token as SHA-256 hash + session row (device, ip)
        I->>K: audit.recorded (login)
        I-->>B: access JWT 30 min + refresh token 7 d + user profile
    end

    Note over B,I: Later, silently at 80% of the access lifetime
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/refresh {refreshToken}
    G->>I: forward (limit 50/s)
    I->>DB: look up hash
    alt token valid and not used
        I->>DB: revoke it, issue a new one (session_id kept)
        I-->>B: new access + refresh
    else token already used (copied)
        I->>DB: revoke the whole token family
        I-->>B: 401 session ended
    else token replaced by a newer login
        I-->>B: 401 signed in on another device
    end
